  "docs.d0051": "File requirements",
  "docs.d0052": "1. The form must include a file field named file. If several are provided, only the first is used.\n2. The extension must be .mp3, .wav, .ogg, or .flac (case-insensitive). Otherwise, returns 400 with the received extension in the error message.\n3. The platform reads the initial file bytes to check for audio content. If the extension does not match the actual content, returns 400 with a message such as `unsupported upload format: file \"a.mp3\" does not look like audio content (detected ...)`.\n4. The entire request, including audio and other form fields, must not exceed 25 MiB. Oversized or malformed forms return 400: `the request body is not a valid multipart upload, or is over the size limit`.",
  "docs.d0053": "Parameter validation",
  "docs.d0054": "model is required. response_format must be json or text; other values return 400: `response_format must be \"json\" or \"text\"; srt, vtt and verbose_json are not supported`. If temperature cannot be parsed as a number, returns 400: `temperature must be a number`.\n\nlanguage, prompt, and temperature are optional; blank values are treated as omitted.",
  "docs.d0055": "Error code reference",
  "docs.d0056": "400 invalid_request: invalid request format or parameters (see above).\n404 model_not_found: the requested model is currently unavailable.\n\nUpstream failures use the following rules (error.code in the OpenAI error format is shown in parentheses):\n\n400: the request cannot be processed (invalid_config / protocol_error), or the selected model does not support it (capability_unsupported)\n429: no capacity is currently available; try again later (rate_limited / backpressure)\n502: the backend returned an error (upstream_error)\n503: the service is temporarily unavailable (connection_failed / runtime_closed)\n504: request timed out (timeout)\n413: the response exceeds the size limit (response_too_large)\n500: another internal error (internal_error)",
  "docs.d0057": "Authentication & quotas",
  "docs.d0058": "All requests require `Bearer {{API_KEY}}` in the Authorization header. A missing, malformed, revoked, or expired Key returns 401 invalid_api_key. If the platform cannot validate the Key temporarily, it returns 503 verification_unavailable; the Key itself may be entirely valid, so try again later.\n\nTenant quotas apply to the tenant owning the Key. Exceeding a quota returns 429, with error.code identifying the exceeded limit: requests_per_minute (requests per minute), tokens_per_minute (tokens per minute), or max_concurrent (concurrent requests). The Retry-After response header suggests how many seconds to wait (at least 1 second).\n\nEvery response includes an X-Request-Id header; provide this value when troubleshooting.",
