  "docs.d0138": "Example: multi-turn conversation",
  "docs.d0139": "The API itself does not retain context. For a multi-turn conversation, include past user and assistant messages in messages in order, then append the current user message.",
  "docs.d0140": "Example: tool calls",
  "docs.d0141": "Declare functions in tools. When the model chooses to call one, finish_reason is tool_calls, and message.tool_calls contains the function name and arguments. After executing the function, append both the model's assistant message (including tool_calls) and a result message with role set to tool and the matching tool_call_id to messages, then send another request.",
  "docs.d0142": "Example: image input",
  "docs.d0143": "content may be an array of content parts mixing text and image_url. Returns 400 (capability_unsupported) if the selected model does not support image input.",
  "docs.d0144": "Parameter restrictions for Claude models",
  "docs.d0145": "When calling Claude models, this API validates parameters more strictly. Violations return 400 (code: unsupported_parameter):\n\n1. Only the parameters listed above are accepted. Other fields, such as n, parallel_tool_calls, reasoning_effort, and prompt_cache_key, are rejected; store may only be false.\n\n2. max_tokens defaults to 4096, with a range of 1 to 64000. temperature ranges from 0 to 1. top_p, seed, stop, and response_format are not supported.\n\n3. tool_choice supports only \"auto\". tools supports only the function type, and function.strict must not be true.\n\n4. Only plain-text content is supported; image and audio parts are not supported. system / developer messages must be at the beginning of the conversation, and at least one user message is required.\n\n5. Request bodies must not exceed 1 MB; larger bodies return 413 (request_too_large).\n\nOther models do not reject unlisted fields, but those fields have no effect.",
  "docs.d0146": "Error code details",
  "docs.d0147": "All error responses use the OpenAI format: {\"error\": {\"message\", \"type\", \"code\"}}. Distinguish errors using the HTTP status and code field.\n\n400: invalid JSON request body (invalid_json), missing required fields or invalid field values (invalid_request), unsupported parameters (unsupported_parameter), or a request unsupported by the selected model (capability_unsupported).\n\n401: missing or invalid API Key (invalid_api_key).\n\n404: the requested model is currently unavailable (model_not_found).\n\n413: the response exceeds the size limit (response_too_large).\n\n429: tenant quota exceeded, with code requests_per_minute / tokens_per_minute / max_concurrent and a Retry-After response header suggesting how many seconds to wait; or temporarily unavailable capacity (rate_limited / backpressure), which can be retried later.\n\n500 / 502: internal service error (internal_error) or an error returned by the upstream model (upstream_error).\n\n503: temporary inability to validate the API Key (verification_unavailable), or temporary service unavailability (connection_failed / runtime_closed).\n\n504: request timed out (timeout).\n\nEvery response includes an X-Request-Id header; include it when reporting an issue.",
  "docs.d0148": "Chat Completions (streaming)",
  "docs.d0149": "An OpenAI Chat Completions-compatible chat API. With stream=true, returns generated content incrementally over SSE.",
  "docs.d0150": "SSE streaming output: each event is a line of data: {chunk}, ending with data: [DONE]",
  "docs.d0151": "Usage statistics are returned with the final chunk",
  "docs.d0152": "Once streaming starts, the HTTP status is fixed at 200. If generation fails mid-stream, the stream ends with a chunk whose finish_reason is error (for Claude models, data: {\"error\": {...}}), without [DONE]. Clients should use this to determine whether the response is complete.",
  "docs.d0153": "Whether to return an SSE stream. Must be true for this page.",
  "docs.d0154": "Completion ID; identical across all chunks in one request.",
  "docs.d0155": "Always chat.completion.chunk.",
  "docs.d0156": "Incremental results; currently always one element. Empty in the usage chunk for Claude models.",
  "docs.d0157": "This increment.",
  "docs.d0158": "assistant in the first chunk.",
  "docs.d0159": "New text fragment.",
  "docs.d0160": "Incremental tool calls: the first fragment contains id, type, and function.name; later fragments append function.arguments.",
  "docs.d0161": "Tool call index.",
  "docs.d0162": "Function name and argument fragments (name, arguments).",
  "docs.d0163": "Finish reason; null while generating. Common values: stop, length, tool_calls; error if the stream fails mid-way.",
  "docs.d0164": "Usage statistics; appear only in chunks where the model reports usage.",
  "docs.d0165": "Output token count.",
  "docs.d0166": "Success (SSE stream)",
  "docs.d0167": "Failure mid-stream",
  "docs.d0168": "Key validation temporarily unavailable",
  "docs.d0169": "SSE format",
  "docs.d0170": "The response Content-Type is text/event-stream. Each event is data: <JSON>, with a blank line between events. Concatenate choices[0].delta.content from each chunk in order to obtain the full reply. Tool call function.arguments must also be concatenated in order. data: [DONE] indicates normal completion.",
  "docs.d0171": "Embeddings & reranking",
